When demos show sparse markers receiving copies of an embedded motif, distinguish the motif's bounding-box origin from the motif coordinate aligned with a marker. Represent that alignment as a signed offset and validate it against multiple marker/copy pairs. Replay every marker footprint against the complete demo output, including source motif retention, overlaps, clipping, and unchanged candidate markers.

A common failure is to shift a plausible template by intuition (top-left, center, or a salient source pixel) without validating the anchor. After incorrect feedback, discard that placement hypothesis and re-derive the offset from observed coordinate correspondences. Validate serialization independently: row widths and legal values must be checked before submission.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen-4/play/users/u043/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-stream-demo-discipline/references/marker-anchor-offsets.md"}

